{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Sally in Continental Europe", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "E-mailing Vanessa", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Present Continuous vs. Going To for the Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Continuous tense for things that are booked in the future.  This can be a hotel reservation or an appointment with a doctor.<br>  <br>You use <span class=\"italic\">Going to + verb</span> to talk about intentions. These are things you want to do in the future. There is no booking or appointment.<br>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Going To\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm coming back home to New York.<br>   <br>I'm taking a small tour with some nice people tomorrow.<br></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm going to call you soon. <br>   <br>John is going to arrive in Mexico any day now.<br></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Zero Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the Simple Present tense in a zero conditional sentence.<br> <br><span class=\"italic\">When</span> can often take the place of <span class=\"italic\">if</span>.<br>  <br>You can use the Imperative with a zero conditional sentence.<br>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If you don't write, I get worried!   (Simple Present)<br>When you don't write, I get worried! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you get a chance, come here. (Imperative)<br>When you get a chance, come here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you like flowers, Holland is the country to visit.<br> When you like flowers, Holland is the country to visit.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "worried", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling anxious and upset", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I get worried when you don't e-mail me!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le10ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk to friends.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "a line or two", "type": "name"}, {"content": "one or two written sentences", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Please write a line or two so I know you are okay!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le10ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "any day now", "type": "name"}, {"content": "sometime soon", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are leaving any day now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le10ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "field", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an open space in the countryside  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are fields and fields of tulips near Amsterdam! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le10ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "ever", "type": "name"}, {"content": "at any time ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you ever go out for pizza?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le10ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "That's nothing new!", "type": "name"}, {"content": "this happens all the time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She's late again? That's nothing new!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le10ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "girl trouble", "type": "name"}, {"content": "romantic problems with girls", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He always has some girl trouble!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le10ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn4le10ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "You are away from home. Write an e-mail to a friend.", "type": "